% -v reports what evaluation did.  Only the derived-fact count is
% pinned here: it is a property of the least model and so is the same under
% both engines, while the iteration and scan counts are what -D semi is meant
% to reduce.
edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).

path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- edge(X, Y), path(Y, Z).
